<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch bond yield survey - January.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch bond yield survey - January.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters continues its monthly survey of bank economists' forecasts of levels for key Dutch interest rates in one month's time. Tabulated results follow:</p>
<p>		     3-MTH   5-YR   10-YR   LONG    5-YR   10-YR</p>
<p>							     SPREAD  SPREAD</p>
<p>							     (to Bunds, bp)</p>
<p>CURRENT	    3.01    4.60   5.62    6.44     -5     -13</p>
<p>ABN AMRO</p>
<p>HOARE GOVETT     2.90    4.70   5.70    6.50    -10     -17</p>
<p>GENERALE BANK    3.00    4.70   5.65    6.35    -10     -15</p>
<p>ING BARINGS	3.00    4.65   5.75    6.50     -5     -10</p>
<p>IRIS		 3.00    4.50   5.60    6.45    -10	-5</p>
<p>MEESPIERSON	3.05    4.40   5.55    6.40    -12     -15</p>
<p>RABOBANK</p>
<p>INTERNATIONAL    3.00    4.70   5.70    6.50     -5     -10</p>
<p>NOTES - The relevant benchmark bonds are the 8.75 pct Sept 15, 2001, 6.0 pct Jan 15, 2006 and 7.5 pct Jan 5, 2023 Dutch state loans (DSLs) and the 8.25 pct Sept 20, 2001 and 6.25 pct April 26, 2006 Bunds.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000, fax 31 20 504 5040</p>
